<!-- SECTION 15A: LEGAL FRAMEWORK -->
<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework: GST Returns Under CGST Act 2017</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p><strong>Governing Act:</strong> Central Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017 + Delhi Goods and Services Tax Act, 2017</p><p><strong>GSTR-1:</strong> Section 37. Monthly by 11th or Quarterly (QRMP) by 13th.</p><p><strong>GSTR-3B:</strong> Section 39. Monthly by 20th or Quarterly 22nd/24th. Delhi = Category 2 (24th).</p><p><strong>QRMP:</strong> Notification 84/2020. Turnover up to Rs 5 crore. Monthly PMT-06 by 25th. IFF for B2B in Month 1/2.</p><p><strong>Late Fee:</strong> Section 47. Rs 50/day. Nil: Rs 20/day. Capped Rs 5,000.</p><p><strong>Interest:</strong> Section 50. 18% p.a. on delayed tax. 24% on excess ITC claimed wrongly.</p><p><strong>Sequential Filing:</strong> Rule 61(4). Current period blocked until previous filed.</p><p><strong>3-Year Lock:</strong> From July 2025, GSTR-3B cannot be filed after 3 years from due date.</p><p><strong>Source:</strong> <a href="https://gst.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">gst.gov.in</a>, <a href="https://cbic.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">cbic.gov.in</a></p>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- FAQ SECTION -->
<section id="faq-section" class="content-section" style="background-color: #ffffff;">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <div class="faq-expanded">
                <aside class="faq-expanded__aside">
                    <h2 class="faq-expanded__title">FAQs: GST Returns in Delhi</h2>
                    <p class="faq-expanded__lead">Common questions about GST return filing deadlines, QRMP scheme, and compliance for Delhi businesses.</p>
                    @include('partials.faq-enquiry-form', ['enquiryLocation' => 'Delhi', 'enquiryService' => 'GST Returns in Delhi'])
                </aside>
                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What are the GST return due dates for Delhi businesses?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Monthly filers: GSTR-1 by 11th and GSTR-3B by 20th of the following month. QRMP quarterly filers: GSTR-1 by 13th after the quarter end and GSTR-3B by 24th (Delhi is Category 2). QRMP monthly tax payment (PMT-06) by 25th. IFF (optional B2B upload) by 13th in Month 1 and 2. Patron files well before each deadline.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the QRMP scheme and does it apply in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>QRMP allows businesses with turnover up to Rs 5 crore to file GSTR-1 and GSTR-3B quarterly while making monthly estimated tax payments via PMT-06 by the 25th. Delhi falls under Category 2, so quarterly GSTR-3B is due by the 24th (not 22nd). IFF allows quarterly filers to upload B2B invoices in Month 1 and 2 so buyers can claim ITC sooner.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is the penalty for late GST return filing in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Late fee: Rs 50 per day (Rs 25 CGST + Rs 25 Delhi SGST) per return, capped at Rs 5,000. For Nil returns: Rs 20 per day, capped at Rs 500. Interest: 18% per annum on unpaid tax from day after due date. Sequential filing block: missing one month cascades penalties across all subsequent months.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I file Nil GST return in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Yes. If zero transactions in a month, you must still file Nil GSTR-1 and Nil GSTR-3B. Nil returns can be filed via portal or SMS. Failure to file attracts Rs 20/day late fee and blocks subsequent filings.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is GSTR-2B and why is it important?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>GSTR-2B is a static, auto-populated ITC statement generated on the 14th of each month showing available ITC based on suppliers' GSTR-1/IFF filings. Before filing GSTR-3B, reconcile purchase register with GSTR-2B to ensure no excess or missed ITC. Patron runs this reconciliation before every GSTR-3B filing.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What happens if I miss one month's GST return?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Sequential filing rule means you cannot file the current month until all previous months are filed. Missing January blocks February, March, and all subsequent months. Late fee accumulates at Rs 50/day per unfiled return. A single missed month creates thousands in penalties within weeks.</p></div>
                    </div>
